  "slug": "melanoma-early-melanoma-5860",
  "summary": "Recent benchmarks and statistical analyses show that dataset properties and marker statistics, not only algorithm choice, drive single-cell inference outcomes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is evaluation of computational methods for single-cell and omics data, with attention to what drives observed performance. A benchmark of 63 scRNA-seq cell-type annotation tools reports that dataset separability (kNN purity) explains most accuracy variance. A marker-discovery analysis finds that Wilcoxon marker scores scale with cluster size (r~0.90-0.95), so DE-nominated markers are less cluster-specific than expected. A metacell model predicts Gaussian mixture structure in PCA space and is tested on real data. Software contributions address specific problems: scXMatch for distribution-shift testing, LOL for leakage-aware phenotype prediction, Ryder for epigenome normalization, and STiLE and Serval for spatial transcriptomics. Protocol and design papers cover methylation sequencing best practices and hashtag-multiplexing trade-offs. The new contribution is the explicit attribution of performance to data structure rather than method choice.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-04"
}
